      "text": "To fix this, we need to transition from \"finding a safe Y level\" to **validating the entire path**. \n\nThe implementation below fixes the issue by:\n1.  **Full Path Validation:** Checking all three segments of a path (Vertical-Horizontal-Vertical) for collisions before accepting a route.\n2.  **Gutter Routing:** If nodes are in the same column but another node is between them, the line will now \"step out\" into the empty space (gutter) between columns.\n3.  **Collision Helper:** Adding a unified segment checker to prevent redundant code.\n\nReplace your existing `buildObstacleFreePath`, `routeForVerticalApproach`, `routeForHorizontalApproach`, and `findSafeHorizontalCorridor` with the following implementation:\n\n```kotlin\n    /**\n     * Builds a path from start to approach point to end, avoiding all obstacles.\n     */\n    private fun buildObstacleFreePath(\n        start: Offset,\n        approach: Offset,\n        end: Offset,\n        endSide: NodeSide,\n        fromOrganName: String,\n        toOrganName: String,\n        nodePositions: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e,\n        fromPosition: NodePosition,\n        toPosition: NodePosition,\n        isBackEdge: Boolean\n    ): List\u003cOffset\u003e {\n        val waypoints \u003d mutableListOf\u003cOffset\u003e()\n        waypoints.add(start)\n\n        // 1. Handle Back Edges (Route to the far right gutter)\n        if (isBackEdge) {\n            val margin \u003d 60f\n            val sideX \u003d max(fromPosition.x + fromPosition.width, toPosition.x + toPosition.width) + margin\n            waypoints.add(Offset(start.x, start.y + 20f)) // Step down\n            waypoints.add(Offset(sideX, start.y + 20f))    // To right side\n            waypoints.add(Offset(sideX, approach.y))       // Up/Down to approach height\n            waypoints.add(approach)\n            waypoints.add(end)\n            return waypoints\n        }\n\n        // 2. Handle same-column vertical obstacles (S-Curve routing)\n        // If they are aligned vertically but something is in between\n        if (kotlin.math.abs(start.x - approach.x) \u003c 10f) {\n            if (isSegmentBlocked(start, approach, fromOrganName, toOrganName, nodePositions)) {\n                // Shift the path into the \"gutter\" between columns\n                val gutterShift \u003d (NODE_WIDTH / 2) + (HORIZONTAL_NODE_SPACING / 2)\n                val gutterX \u003d start.x + gutterShift\n                \n                waypoints.add(Offset(start.x, start.y + 20f))\n                waypoints.add(Offset(gutterX, start.y + 20f))\n                waypoints.add(Offset(gutterX, approach.y))\n                waypoints.add(approach)\n                waypoints.add(end)\n                return waypoints\n            }\n        }\n\n        // 3. Find a safe 3-segment path (Down -\u003e Across -\u003e Approach)\n        val safePath \u003d findSafeMultiSegmentPath(\n            start, approach, fromOrganName, toOrganName, nodePositions\n        )\n        \n        waypoints.addAll(safePath)\n        waypoints.add(end)\n        return waypoints\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Tries several Y-levels to find a path where all three orthogonal segments are clear.\n     */\n    private fun findSafeMultiSegmentPath(\n        start: Offset,\n        approach: Offset,\n        fromName: String,\n        toName: String,\n        nodePositions: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e\n    ): List\u003cOffset\u003e {\n        // Potential Y-levels to try for the horizontal segment\n        val verticalStepOut \u003d 30f\n        val possibleYLevels \u003d listOf(\n            start.y + verticalStepOut,               // Just below source\n            approach.y,                              // Aligned with approach\n            (start.y + approach.y) / 2,              // Halfway between\n            start.y + verticalStepOut + 40f,         // Further down\n            approach.y - 40f                         // Slightly above approach\n        )\n\n        for (testY in possibleYLevels) {\n            val p1 \u003d Offset(start.x, testY)\n            val p2 \u003d Offset(approach.x, testY)\n\n            // Segment 1: Vertical down from start\n            val seg1Clear \u003d !isSegmentBlocked(start, p1, fromName, toName, nodePositions)\n            // Segment 2: Horizontal across\n            val seg2Clear \u003d !isSegmentBlocked(p1, p2, fromName, toName, nodePositions)\n            // Segment 3: Vertical to approach\n            val seg3Clear \u003d !isSegmentBlocked(p2, approach, fromName, toName, nodePositions)\n\n            if (seg1Clear \u0026\u0026 seg2Clear \u0026\u0026 seg3Clear) {\n                return listOf(p1, p2, approach)\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Fallback: If no perfect path is found, use the first guess \n        // but it\u0027s much less likely to happen with this multi-check logic\n        return listOf(Offset(start.x, start.y + verticalStepOut), Offset(approach.x, start.y + verticalStepOut), approach)\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Checks if a specific line segment is blocked by any node (except source/destination).\n     */\n    private fun isSegmentBlocked(\n        p1: Offset,\n        p2: Offset,\n        ignore1: String,\n        ignore2: String,\n        nodePositions: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e\n    ): Boolean {\n        for ((name, pos) in nodePositions) {\n            if (name \u003d\u003d ignore1 || name \u003d\u003d ignore2) continue\n            // Using a slightly larger margin for the path check than the node itself\n            if (lineSegmentIntersectsNode(p1.x, p1.y, p2.x, p2.y, pos, margin \u003d 15f)) {\n                return true\n            }\n        }\n        return false\n    }\n```\n\n### Key Improvements made:\n\n1.  **Segment Validation (`isSegmentBlocked`):** Your previous code only checked if the horizontal \"corridor\" was safe. This new version checks the vertical lines dropping down from the source node too. This prevents the line from going through a node directly underneath the source.\n2.  **S-Curve Routing:** Added a specific check for nodes in the same column. If a straight vertical line is blocked, it calculates a `gutterX` (midway between the current column and the next) and routes the line through that empty space.\n3.  **Adaptive Y-Levels:** `findSafeMultiSegmentPath` tests multiple scenarios (like routing immediately under the source vs. routing at the height of the destination) and picks the first one that has zero collisions on all segments.\n4.  **Buffer Management:** Increased the intersection margin slightly and ensured the \"Step Out\" distance (20f-30f) is large enough to move the line away from the source node\u0027s collision box before it turns.",
