      "text": "The reason your lines are still drawing through the middle of nodes on the same row is that your routing logic considers the **center height of the node** (`approach.y`) as a valid candidate for the horizontal path.\n\nBecause the source and destination nodes are **ignored** in your collision check (`if (name \u003d\u003d ignore1 || name \u003d\u003d ignore2) continue`), the engine sees a straight path through the middle of the nodes as \"safe\" if no *other* nodes are in the way.\n\n### The Fix: \"Gutter-First\" Routing\nTo fix this, we need to:\n1.  **Restrict Corridor Candidates:** For nodes on the same row, we must only allow horizontal segments to exist in the \"gutters\" (the vertical space between rows).\n2.  **Explicit Vertical Step-out:** Force the line to exit the node\u0027s bounding box vertically before it is allowed to move horizontally.\n3.  **Refined Collision Logic:** Ensure that even if we ignore the source/dest node names, we don\u0027t pick a Y-coordinate that is within the height of the row itself.\n\nHere is the updated `GraphLayoutEngine.kt` with the improved same-row routing and collision logic.\n\n```kotlin\npackage jon.sharp.metabolism.simulator.ui.canvas\n\nimport androidx.compose.ui.geometry.Offset\nimport androidx.compose.ui.geometry.Size\nimport androidx.compose.ui.graphics.Color\nimport jon.sharp.metabolism.simulator.model.body.OrganLayoutConfig\nimport kotlin.math.max\nimport kotlin.math.abs\nimport kotlin.math.atan2\n\n/**\n * Represents the four sides of a node for edge connections.\n */\nenum class NodeSide {\n    TOP, BOTTOM, LEFT, RIGHT\n}\n\nfun getConnectionPoint(position: NodePosition, side: NodeSide, offset: Float \u003d 0f): Offset {\n    return when (side) {\n        NodeSide.TOP -\u003e Offset(position.x + (position.width / 2) + offset, position.y)\n        NodeSide.BOTTOM -\u003e Offset(position.x + (position.width / 2) + offset, position.y + position.height)\n        NodeSide.LEFT -\u003e Offset(position.x, position.y + (position.height / 2))\n        NodeSide.RIGHT -\u003e Offset(position.x + position.width, position.y + (position.height / 2))\n    }\n}\n\nfun determineDestinationSide(fromOrganName: String, toOrganName: String, fromRow: Int, toRow: Int): NodeSide {\n    val fromCol \u003d OrganLayoutConfig.getColumnNumber(fromOrganName)\n    val toCol \u003d OrganLayoutConfig.getColumnNumber(toOrganName)\n    return when {\n        fromRow \u003c toRow -\u003e NodeSide.TOP\n        fromRow \u003e toRow -\u003e if (fromCol \u003e toCol) NodeSide.RIGHT else NodeSide.LEFT\n        else -\u003e if (fromCol \u003e toCol) NodeSide.RIGHT else NodeSide.LEFT // Same row: connect to sides\n    }\n}\n\nfun lineSegmentIntersectsNode(x1: Float, y1: Float, x2: Float, y2: Float, nodePos: NodePosition, margin: Float \u003d 10f): Boolean {\n    val nodeLeft \u003d nodePos.x - margin\n    val nodeRight \u003d nodePos.x + nodePos.width + margin\n    val nodeTop \u003d nodePos.y - margin\n    val nodeBottom \u003d nodePos.y + nodePos.height + margin\n\n    val dx \u003d x2 - x1\n    val dy \u003d y2 - y1\n    if (dx \u003d\u003d 0f \u0026\u0026 dy \u003d\u003d 0f) return x1 \u003e\u003d nodeLeft \u0026\u0026 x1 \u003c\u003d nodeRight \u0026\u0026 y1 \u003e\u003d nodeTop \u0026\u0026 y1 \u003c\u003d nodeBottom\n\n    var t0 \u003d 0f\n    var t1 \u003d 1f\n    val edges \u003d listOf(Pair(-dx, x1 - nodeLeft), Pair(dx, nodeRight - x1), Pair(-dy, y1 - nodeTop), Pair(dy, nodeBottom - y1))\n\n    for ((p, q) in edges) {\n        if (p \u003d\u003d 0f) { if (q \u003c 0f) return false } \n        else {\n            val r \u003d q / p\n            if (p \u003c 0f) { if (r \u003e t1) return false; if (r \u003e t0) t0 \u003d r } \n            else { if (r \u003c t0) return false; if (r \u003c t1) t1 \u003d r }\n        }\n    }\n    return t0 \u003c\u003d t1\n}\n\nclass GraphLayoutEngine(private val nodes: List\u003cGraphNodeWithMetabolites\u003e, private val availableWidth: Float) {\n    companion object {\n        const val NODE_WIDTH \u003d 260f\n        const val NODE_MIN_HEIGHT \u003d 84f\n        const val HORIZONTAL_NODE_SPACING \u003d 40f\n        const val LAYER_SPACING \u003d 120f\n        const val CANVAS_PADDING \u003d 60f\n        private val COLOR_PALETTE \u003d listOf(Color(0xFF6B9BD1), Color(0xFF8CC152), Color(0xFFFFCE54), Color(0xFFFC6E51), Color(0xFFAC92EC))\n        private fun getNodeColor(index: Int): Color \u003d COLOR_PALETTE[index % COLOR_PALETTE.size]\n    }\n\n    fun computeLayout(): LayoutResult {\n        if (nodes.isEmpty()) return LayoutResult(emptyMap(), emptyList(), 0f, 0f)\n        val layerMap \u003d nodes.associate { it.organName to it.rowNumber }\n        val (nodePositions, nodeColorMap) \u003d calculateVerticalNodePositions(layerMap)\n        val edgePaths \u003d calculateEdgePaths(nodePositions, layerMap, nodeColorMap)\n        val bounds \u003d calculateCanvasBounds(nodePositions)\n        return LayoutResult(nodePositions, edgePaths, bounds.width, bounds.height)\n    }\n\n    private fun calculateVerticalNodePositions(layerMap: Map\u003cString, Int\u003e): Pair\u003cMap\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e, Map\u003cString, Color\u003e\u003e {\n        val positions \u003d mutableMapOf\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e()\n        val colorMap \u003d mutableMapOf\u003cString, Color\u003e()\n        val layers \u003d nodes.groupBy { layerMap[it.organName] ?: 0 }.toSortedMap()\n        \n        val maxCols \u003d layers.values.maxOfOrNull { it.size } ?: 1\n        val totalWidth \u003d (maxCols * NODE_WIDTH) + ((maxCols - 1) * HORIZONTAL_NODE_SPACING)\n        val startX \u003d (availableWidth - totalWidth) / 2\n\n        var currentY \u003d CANVAS_PADDING\n        layers.forEach { (_, nodesInLayer) -\u003e\n            nodesInLayer.sortedBy { OrganLayoutConfig.getColumnNumber(it.organName) }.forEachIndexed { idx, node -\u003e\n                val x \u003d startX + (idx * (NODE_WIDTH + HORIZONTAL_NODE_SPACING))\n                val color \u003d getNodeColor(positions.size)\n                positions[node.organName] \u003d NodePosition(node.organName, x, currentY, NODE_WIDTH, NODE_MIN_HEIGHT, color)\n                colorMap[node.organName] \u003d color\n            }\n            currentY +\u003d NODE_MIN_HEIGHT + LAYER_SPACING\n        }\n        return Pair(positions, colorMap)\n    }\n\n    private fun calculateEdgePaths(nodePositions: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e, layerMap: Map\u003cString, Int\u003e, nodeColorMap: Map\u003cString, Color\u003e): List\u003cEdgePath\u003e {\n        val edgePaths \u003d mutableListOf\u003cEdgePath\u003e()\n        nodes.forEach { sourceNode -\u003e\n            sourceNode.edges.forEach { edge -\u003e\n                val fromPos \u003d nodePositions[sourceNode.organName] ?: return@forEach\n                val toPos \u003d nodePositions[edge.destinationName] ?: return@forEach\n                val fromLayer \u003d layerMap[sourceNode.organName] ?: 0\n                val toLayer \u003d layerMap[edge.destinationName] ?: 0\n                \n                // Grouping offset for parallel lines\n                val siblingEdges \u003d sourceNode.edges.filter { it.destinationName \u003d\u003d edge.destinationName }\n                val edgeIndex \u003d siblingEdges.indexOf(edge)\n                val offset \u003d if (siblingEdges.size \u003e 1) (edgeIndex - (siblingEdges.size - 1) / 2f) * 15f else 0f\n\n                val waypoints \u003d calculateOrthogonalWaypoints(\n                    sourceNode.organName, edge.destinationName, fromPos, toPos,\n                    fromLayer, toLayer, toLayer \u003c\u003d fromLayer, offset, nodePositions\n                )\n                edgePaths.add(EdgePath(sourceNode.organName, edge.destinationName, toLayer \u003c\u003d fromLayer, waypoints, nodeColorMap[sourceNode.organName] ?: Color.Gray, edge.metabolites))\n            }\n        }\n        return edgePaths\n    }\n\n    private fun calculateOrthogonalWaypoints(\n        fromName: String, toName: String, fromPos: NodePosition, toPos: NodePosition,\n        fromRow: Int, toRow: Int, isBackEdge: Boolean, offset: Float, nodePositions: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e\n    ): List\u003cOffset\u003e {\n        val start \u003d getConnectionPoint(fromPos, NodeSide.BOTTOM, offset)\n        val side \u003d determineDestinationSide(fromName, toName, fromRow, toRow)\n        val end \u003d getConnectionPoint(toPos, side, offset)\n\n        // The approach point is 30px away from the destination connection side\n        val approach \u003d when (side) {\n            NodeSide.TOP -\u003e Offset(end.x, end.y - 30f)\n            NodeSide.BOTTOM -\u003e Offset(end.x, end.y + 30f)\n            NodeSide.LEFT -\u003e Offset(end.x - 30f, end.y)\n            NodeSide.RIGHT -\u003e Offset(end.x + 30f, end.y)\n        }\n\n        val waypoints \u003d mutableListOf(start)\n\n        // BACK EDGES or SAME ROW: Always route via the gutter to avoid crossing nodes\n        if (isBackEdge || fromRow \u003d\u003d toRow) {\n            val gutterY \u003d if (fromRow \u003d\u003d toRow) start.y + (LAYER_SPACING / 2) else min(start.y, approach.y) - (LAYER_SPACING / 2)\n            val sideX \u003d if (isBackEdge) max(fromPos.x + fromPos.width, toPos.x + toPos.width) + 60f else approach.x\n            \n            waypoints.add(Offset(start.x, gutterY))\n            waypoints.add(Offset(sideX, gutterY))\n            waypoints.add(Offset(sideX, approach.y))\n        } else {\n            // FORWARD EDGES: Find a safe multi-segment path\n            val path \u003d findSafePath(start, approach, fromName, toName, nodePositions)\n            waypoints.addAll(path)\n        }\n\n        waypoints.add(approach)\n        waypoints.add(end)\n        return waypoints\n    }\n\n    private fun findSafePath(start: Offset, approach: Offset, from: String, to: String, nodes: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e): List\u003cOffset\u003e {\n        val stepOutY \u003d start.y + 30f\n        val midY \u003d (start.y + approach.y) / 2f\n        \n        // Prioritize paths that don\u0027t share Y-levels with node centers\n        val candidates \u003d listOf(stepOutY, midY, approach.y - 30f)\n        \n        for (testY in candidates) {\n            val p1 \u003d Offset(start.x, testY)\n            val p2 \u003d Offset(approach.x, testY)\n            if (!isBlocked(start, p1, from, to, nodes) \u0026\u0026 \n                !isBlocked(p1, p2, from, to, nodes) \u0026\u0026 \n                !isBlocked(p2, approach, from, to, nodes)) {\n                return listOf(p1, p2)\n            }\n        }\n        return listOf(Offset(start.x, stepOutY), Offset(approach.x, stepOutY))\n    }\n\n    private fun isBlocked(p1: Offset, p2: Offset, ignore1: String, ignore2: String, nodes: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e): Boolean {\n        return nodes.any { (name, pos) -\u003e \n            name !\u003d ignore1 \u0026\u0026 name !\u003d ignore2 \u0026\u0026 lineSegmentIntersectsNode(p1.x, p1.y, p2.x, p2.y, pos, margin \u003d 15f)\n        }\n    }\n\n    private fun calculateCanvasBounds(nodePositions: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e): Size {\n        val maxX \u003d nodePositions.values.maxOfOrNull { it.x + it.width } ?: 0f\n        val maxY \u003d nodePositions.values.maxOfOrNull { it.y + it.height } ?: 0f\n        return Size(maxX + CANVAS_PADDING, maxY + CANVAS_PADDING)\n    }\n}\n\nfun calculateLabelPosition(waypoints: List\u003cOffset\u003e): Offset {\n    if (waypoints.size \u003c 2) return waypoints.firstOrNull() ?: Offset.Zero\n    // Find the longest horizontal segment for the label\n    var bestSeg \u003d Pair(waypoints[0], waypoints[1])\n    var maxDist \u003d -1f\n    for (i in 0 until waypoints.size - 1) {\n        val d \u003d abs(waypoints[i].x - waypoints[i+1].x)\n        if (abs(waypoints[i].y - waypoints[i+1].y) \u003c 1f \u0026\u0026 d \u003e maxDist) {\n            maxDist \u003d d\n            bestSeg \u003d Pair(waypoints[i], waypoints[i+1])\n        }\n    }\n    return Offset((bestSeg.first.x + bestSeg.second.x) / 2, bestSeg.first.y - 10f)\n}\n\nfun calculateArrowAngle(x1: Float, y1: Float, x2: Float, y2: Float): Float \u003d atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1)\n```\n\n### Key Changes:\n1.  **Same-Row Gutter Enforcement:** In `calculateOrthogonalWaypoints`, if `fromRow \u003d\u003d toRow`, the engine now **ignores** the center-line path entirely. It calculates a `gutterY` exactly halfway between the current row and the row below (`start.y + LAYER_SPACING / 2`). This ensures the horizontal line always travels through the empty vertical space between layers.\n2.  **Strict Forward-Edge Validation:** `findSafePath` now checks all three segments of the path. It also prioritizes `stepOutY` (30px below the source node) over the center-line height, which prevents the \"cutting through the corner\" effect.\n3.  **Corrected Side Connections:** For same-row nodes, `determineDestinationSide` now correctly identifies whether to hit the `LEFT` or `RIGHT` side based on column numbers, ensuring the line wraps around and hits the side of the node instead of trying to hit the top/bottom while traveling horizontally.\n4.  **Collision Margin:** I increased the `CANVAS_PADDING` and collision `margin` to 15f to ensure lines don\u0027t \"hug\" the nodes too tightly.",
