sortedSegments) {\n        val midX \u003d (segment.first.x + segment.second.x) / 2\n        val y \u003d segment.first.y\n        \n        // Check if a label placed here (above the line) would hit any node\n        val labelRectTop \u003d y - labelHeight - 15f \n        val labelRectBottom \u003d y - 5f\n        val labelRectLeft \u003d midX - 50f // Assumed avg width\n        val labelRectRight \u003d midX + 50f\n\n        val overlapsNode \u003d nodePositions.values.any { node -\u003e\n            val nodeLeft \u003d node.x - 10f\n            val nodeRight \u003d node.x + node.width + 10f\n            val nodeTop \u003d node.y - 10f\n            val nodeBottom \u003d node.y + node.height + 10f\n\n            // Rect-Rect intersection check\n            !(labelRectRight \u003c nodeLeft || labelRectLeft \u003e nodeRight || \n              labelRectBottom \u003c nodeTop || labelRectTop \u003e nodeBottom)\n        }\n\n        if (!overlapsNode) {\n            return Offset(midX, y)\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Fallback: If all horizontal segments hit nodes, pick the midpoint of the longest one\n    // and hope for the best, or use the first waypoint\n    val longest \u003d sortedSegments.firstOrNull() ?: return waypoints[waypoints.size / 2]\n    return Offset((longest.first.x + longest.second.x) / 2, longest.first.y)\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Update `drawGraphEdge` in your Drawing code\nYou need to pass the `nodePositions` into the label calculation. You likely have access to these in your main `Canvas` loop or `LayoutResult`.\n\n```kotlin\nfun DrawScope.drawGraphEdge(\n    edgePath: EdgePath,\n    nodePositions: Map\u003cString, NodePosition\u003e, // Add this parameter\n    colorScheme: ColorScheme,\n    textMeasurer: TextMeasurer\n) {\n    val color \u003d edgePath.color\n    val waypoints \u003d edgePath.waypoints\n    if (waypoints.size \u003c 2) return\n\n    // Draw the lines\n    for (i in 0 until waypoints.size - 1) {\n        drawLine(color \u003d color, start \u