 0.3f),\n        topLeft \u003d boxTopLeft + Offset(2f, 2f),\n        size \u003d Size(boxWidth, boxHeight),\n        cornerRadius \u003d CornerRadius(4f, 4f)\n    )\n\n    // Draw solid background using the edge color (opaque is better for node-avoidance)\n    drawRoundRect(\n        color \u003d color.copy(alpha \u003d 0.95f),\n        topLeft \u003d boxTopLeft,\n        size \u003d Size(boxWidth, boxHeight),\n        cornerRadius \u003d CornerRadius(4f, 4f)\n    )\n\n    drawText(\n        textLayoutResult \u003d textResult,\n        topLeft \u003d boxTopLeft + Offset(padding, padding)\n    )\n}\n```\n\n### Why this works:\n1.  **Gutter Preference:** By checking the `overlapsNode` boolean, the engine will skip horizontal segments that enter or exit a node (like the 30px \"approach\" segments) and instead choose the long segments we created in the **gutters** (the empty vertical space between rows).\n2.  **Opaque Backgrounds:** Changing the label background alpha from `0.85f` to `0.95f` or `1.0f` ensures that if a line *does* pass behind a label, the text remains legible.\n3.  **Strict Y-Check:** The collision check adds a `10f` margin to node boundaries, ensuring labels don\u0027t just \"touch\" nodes but stay a respectful distance away.",
